Local modifications:
  - dkms.conf: adds PATCH[0..4]/PATCH_MATCH[0..4] to apply the local hardening
    patches during the DKMS build (see patches/). DKMS 3.2.2 resolves the
    PATCH[] value below its patches/ directory, so the value is the bare file
    name (e.g. 0001-t2smc-range-checks.patch).  The C source stays pristine so
    upstream re-syncs remain byte-diffable.
  - patches/0001-t2smc-range-checks.patch: local hardening (fan min/target range
    checks against the factory F%dMn/F%dMx envelope captured at probe, battery
    charge-limit value validation, RTC offset range check, modulo-and-sign-extend
    fold).  Adds t2smc_range.h at the DKMS module root at build time only
    (56-t2-dkms.sh flattens src/ into /usr/src/t2smc-0.1/, so the patch is
    written with -p1 paths at the module root).  The rework keeps the pinned
    modulo behaviour for the RTC offset (no upstream semantics change) but
    rejects writes outside the signed 48-bit register range; the fan validator
    captures the factory envelope so the min cannot ratchet upward, validates
    the 64-bit hwmon long before narrowing it to unsigned int, and does not
    read F%dTg for a target write (irrelevant there; a stale/zero or
    unreadable target would otherwise reject an otherwise-valid write).  The
    envelope capture is non-fatal: if the SMC cannot report the limits the
    write path falls back to the live F%dMn/F%dMx.
  - patches/0002-t2smc-temp-discovery-idx.patch: bound temperature-discovery
    idx by the T..U candidate range, not pass-1's success count.  Pass one
    allocates only for successful sp78 entries and skips transient lookups,
    but pass two retries without checking idx; the fix allocates the full
    candidate range and updates temp_count to the actual populated count.
  - patches/0003-t2smc-cache-init.patch: initialise the cache-fill return
    value in t2smc_get_entry_by_index() so the locked goto-out does not
    read an uninitialised int when a second caller observes the cache
    already populated.
  - patches/0004-t2smc-charge-limit-atomic.patch: validate the charge limit
    before the first write and reject values the CHWA-only binary flag cannot
    represent; serialise the full BCLM + CHLS/CHWA transaction under a
    dedicated charge_lock so another setter cannot interleave between the two
    writes.  charge_lock is deliberately not the SMC mailbox mutex: each
    t2smc_write_key() still takes that internally, so holding it across the
    transaction would self-deadlock.  get_charge_limit() takes the same lock
    so it cannot observe BCLM mid-transaction.
  - patches/0005-t2smc-telemetry-robust.patch: saturate the float-telemetry
    shift before it overflows u64, and stop reading from an uninitialised
    value16/signed16 in t2smc_power_show() (the read-failure path returns
    ret without exposing val).
